                <pb facs="0364" n="244" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg244"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Snyder to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-07-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                    1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Snyder reports that a decree has been issued by the Government of Colombia
                    prohibiting the receipt in custom-houses of <hi rendition="#italic">vales
                        extranjeros</hi>, which practically annuls the claims of citizens of the
                    United States.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
